From: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] env: nowhere: add DSB + settle delay before env_set_default on sun5i

On Allwinner sun5i/R8 (C.H.I.P.), U-Boot hangs inside the
himport_r() parse loop when loading the default environment after
NAND initialisation.  The sunxi NAND controller (NFC) enables the
AHB DMA clock gate during hw_init even though all I/O is PIO/SRAM;
combined with the MBUS arbiter state left by NAND BBT scanning,
there appear to be unresolved AHB/MBUS bus transactions that stall
subsequent DRAM accesses from the CPU core.

UART writes target device/strongly-ordered memory, which on ARM926
acts as an implicit Data Synchronisation Barrier -- this explains
why adding debug puts() inside the parse loop eliminates the hang.

Issue an explicit CP15 DSB before env_set_default() to drain all
pending write-buffer and bus transactions, then wait 50 ms for the
AHB/MBUS arbiter to return to idle before beginning the environment
parse.  Without this the parse loop stalls indefinitely after NAND
initialisation on sun5i.

Signed-off-by: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
---
 env/nowhere.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/env/nowhere.c b/env/nowhere.c
--- a/env/nowhere.c
+++ b/env/nowhere.c
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@
 #include <env_internal.h>
 #include <asm/global_data.h>
 #include <linux/stddef.h>
+#include <asm/system.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>

 DECLARE_GLOBAL_DATA_PTR;

@@ -34,8 +36,18 @@
 	 * searches default_environment array in that case.
 	 * For U-Boot proper, import the default environment to allow reload.
 	 */
-	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD))
+	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD)) {
+		/*
+		 * Workaround for sun5i/R8: the AHB/MBUS arbiter retains
+		 * pending transactions after NAND BBT scanning.  Issue a DSB
+		 * to drain the ARM write buffer and wait for the bus to idle
+		 * before calling himport_r(); without this the parse loop
+		 * stalls indefinitely on this SoC.
+		 */
+		dsb();
+		udelay(50000);
 		env_set_default(NULL, 0);
+	}

 	gd->env_valid = ENV_INVALID;
